{number: 164}
{title: Come, Holy Spirit}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Come, Holy Spirit, [Ab] heav'nly [Eb] Dove,
With all Thy quick'ning [Bb7] pow'rs;
[Eb] Kindle a flame of [Ab] sacred [Eb] love
In these cold [Bb7] hearts of [Eb] ours.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Look [Eb] how we grovel [Ab] here be-[Eb] low,
Fond of these earthly [Bb7] toys;
Our [Eb] souls, how heavily [Ab] they [Eb] go
To reach e-[Bb7] ternal [Eb] joys.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
In [Eb] vain we tune our [Ab] formal [Eb] songs,
In vain we strive to [Bb7] rise;
Ho-[Eb] sannas languish [Ab] on our [Eb] tongues,
And our de-[Bb7] votion [Eb] dies.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Dear [Eb] Lord, and shall we [Ab] ever [Eb] live
At this poor dying [Bb7] rate?
Our [Eb] love so faint, so [Ab] cold to [Eb] Thee,
And Thine to [Bb7] us so [Eb] great!
{end_of_verse}
